---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CopyDoi from '../components/CopyDoi.tsx';
---

<BaseLayout title="WiseEvidence — homeopathy research, made explorable">
  <section>
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">WiseEvidence</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
      An open, searchable, structured, AI-assisted and human-curated evidence platform for
      homeopathy research. Find the research, understand what it studied, see what it reported,
      explore its limitations, and follow the original source.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-sm text-slate-500">
      This is an early foundation. The application is being built in documented, testable stages —
      see the <a href="/methodology" class="underline">methodology</a>. No research records are
      published yet.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12" aria-labelledby="distinctions">
    <h2 id="distinctions" class="text-xl font-semibold">Separate questions, kept separate</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
      WiseEvidence never collapses a paper into a single verdict. It keeps distinct dimensions
      distinct, so you can inspect the evidence yourself rather than trusting one score.
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <li class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <strong>Outcome ≠ Evidence Quality</strong>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-500">
          What a study reported is separate from how rigorously it was conducted.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <strong>Outcome ≠ Confidence</strong>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-500">
          A positive result can carry low confidence; a negative one, high confidence.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <strong>Outcome ≠ Criticism</strong>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-500">
          Methodological criticism is not the same thing as a negative outcome.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <strong>Source ≠ Scientific Truth</strong>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-500">
          Indexing a source is not endorsement of its claims. We link to the original, always.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-sm text-slate-500">
      WiseEvidence does not produce an “efficacy score” and does not present study counts as
      scientific certainty.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12" aria-labelledby="try">
    <h2 id="try" class="text-xl font-semibold">A working piece of the foundation</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
      DOI normalization is one of the first shared utilities. The control below runs the real
      normalizer from the <code>@wise-evidence/domain</code> package.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4">
      <CopyDoi client:load />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
